sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant AU as Author or pipeline
    participant GT as Release gate
    participant RG as Evidence register
    participant KG as Kill guards
    participant CL as Clearance registers §21 and §23
    AU->>GT: Submit artefact with its surface and every cited row
    GT->>KG: Evaluate text against every KillGuard and BannedEntry
    KG-->>GT: Pass, or block naming the EV-K row or the §20.4 entry
    GT->>RG: licence query for each row, component and surface, as of now
    RG-->>GT: Allowed, or allowed with a same-sentence condition, or refused
    GT->>RG: basis query for each derived figure
    RG-->>GT: Derivation with inputs, basis and rounding, or none
    GT->>CL: Clearance status for each legal or competitor statement
    CL-->>GT: Cleared entry with owner and date, or not cleared
    alt every check passes
        GT-->>AU: Release with the citation set recorded
    else any check fails
        GT-->>AU: Block naming each failing row, rule and surface
    end
    Note over GT,RG: If the register cannot answer, the gate fails closed. Payroll runs never call the register - they read published rule versions only
